{
  "title": "Periosteal Chondromas",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8019/periosteal-chondromas",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 21 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Periosteal Chondromas are rare, benign, chondrogenic tumors that occur on the surface of long bones, most commonly the proximal humerus. Patients typically present between the ages of 10 and 20 years of age with regional pain secondary to irritation of overlying tendons.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with radiographs showing a well-demarcated, shallow cortical defect with saucerization of the underlying bone.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually observation. Marginal surgical excision of the lesion, including the underlying cortex, is indicated in patients with severe and progressive pain.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occur in **10-20 year-olds**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the surface of long bones (under periosteum) in distal femur, proximal humerus, and proximal femur",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "59% of lesions in **proximal humerus**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**other locations in the hand (metacarpal or phalanges)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "many are **painful** secondary to irritation of tendons",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "well-demarcated, shallow cortical defect",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "punctate mineralization (calcification) in 1/3.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**saucerization of underlying bone**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8019/images/Case%20F%20-%20prox%20tibia%20-%20xray%20-%20Parsons_moved.png",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "radiographs important to differentiate from chondrosarcoma (histology may be similar)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Histology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "similar to enchondroma except for increased cellularity and more malignant looking cells (can look like chondrosarcoma)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**bland hyaline cartilage**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8019/images/Histology%20A_moved.png",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "small **chondroid cells** in **lacunar spaces**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8019/images/Histology%20C_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
